{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 2360566,
  "courseSlug": "sveltejs-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Svelte.js - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14689604",
      "title": "Emitting Custom Events",
      "lectureOrder": 58,
      "videoOrder": 50,
      "sourceHash": "05c3efeb2c8388739e50529a6035c245b04c08bf51811f0cdc311582ba94bad0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.3,
          "end": 5.78,
          "en": "Event forwarding is nice, but of course it's not always the right tool.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.81,
          "end": 12.2,
          "en": "For example, here we have two buttons and of course I can forward the click on Add to Cart with this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 12.2,
          "end": 13.04,
          "en": "syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.19,
          "end": 15.92,
          "en": "But if I do the same here on delete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.18,
          "end": 22.22,
          "en": "You will see that I always fire the same alert no matter which button I click.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.22,
          "end": 27.95,
          "en": "But typically I of course want to do different things here in App svelte, but I got no way to differentiate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 27.95,
          "end": 29.3,
          "en": "which button was clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 29.33,
          "end": 29.75,
          "en": "Okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.75,
          "end": 35.72,
          "en": "I could actually accept the event object and then analyze the target of the event and find out which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.72,
          "end": 36.71,
          "en": "button it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.71,
          "end": 43.46,
          "en": "But that would require us to write a lot of code where we actually analyze the Dom element, maybe analyze",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 43.46,
          "end": 46.01,
          "en": "the caption of the button to find out what to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.04,
          "end": 48.02,
          "en": "It's not really how we want to write code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.14,
          "end": 56.12,
          "en": "Instead, it would be nicer if we had, let's say on Add to Cart, maybe written like this, and then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 56.12,
          "end": 57.95,
          "en": "we could say add to Cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 58.58,
          "end": 61.97,
          "en": "And now let me structure this across multiple lines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 62,
          "end": 67.49,
          "en": "We also have a on delete event here and there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 69.03999999999999,
          "end": 70.81,
          "en": "Let me put this between.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 71.47,
          "end": 73.41,
          "en": "Double quotes there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 73.42,
          "end": 76.87,
          "en": "We then simply throw an alert where I say delete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 76.87,
          "end": 82,
          "en": "And of course in a real app you would really delete it and not just throw the alert, but for demo purposes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 82,
          "end": 82.87,
          "en": "this is fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 82.87,
          "end": 88.3,
          "en": "So it would be nice if we had these two different events, but these are not events built into the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 88.3,
          "end": 93.28,
          "en": "because how would the browser know that this button is about adding something to a cart?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 93.31,
          "end": 96.72999999999999,
          "en": "It's not like the browser reading our caption and understanding it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 96.72999999999999,
          "end": 98.5,
          "en": "This would also be kind of scary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 98.8,
          "end": 103.99000000000001,
          "en": "This is a typical use case where you want to create your own custom event and emit this event to the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 103.99000000000001,
          "end": 107.38,
          "en": "parent component and you can create such an event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 107.38,
          "end": 108.82,
          "en": "You can dispatch your own events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 108.82,
          "end": 112.75,
          "en": "You just need to import something from Svelte.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 112.87,
          "end": 115.47999999999999,
          "en": "Now, we haven't really done this before thus far.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 115.47999999999999,
          "end": 118.27000000000001,
          "en": "We typically always imported our own components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 118.27000000000001,
          "end": 124.21,
          "en": "But svelte, if you have a look at the Package.json file is a dependency of our project and you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 124.21,
          "end": 131.02,
          "en": "import from that dependency simply with this syntax, not dot slash, but simply by just using the package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 131.12,
          "end": 131.45,
          "en": "name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 131.45,
          "end": 136.91,
          "en": "And then this automatically is resolved to have a look at the package that was added in the Node modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 136.91,
          "end": 138.53,
          "en": "folder to this project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 138.71,
          "end": 144.68,
          "en": "Now Svelte has a create event dispatcher function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 144.68,
          "end": 146.87,
          "en": "Make sure you get the name correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 146.87,
          "end": 148.25,
          "en": "The casing does matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 148.25,
          "end": 151.4,
          "en": "So Capital E, capital D, lowercase C at the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 151.4,
          "end": 155.45,
          "en": "And this allows you to create your own event dispatching function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 155.69,
          "end": 161.27,
          "en": "You can store it in a constant which you can name whatever you want, but dispatch makes a lot of sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 161.27,
          "end": 162.56,
          "en": "and you create that event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 162.56,
          "end": 166.49,
          "en": "Dispatcher By simply calling, create event dispatcher like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 166.85,
          "end": 169.16,
          "en": "This here is now a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 169.16,
          "end": 174.86,
          "en": "So create event dispatcher itself returns a function which you can call the function is stored in the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 174.86,
          "end": 178.37,
          "en": "dispatch constant and now here in onClick.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 178.97,
          "end": 180.29,
          "en": "Add to cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 180.32,
          "end": 186.8,
          "en": "We can either assign a in-line handler or we create a full flex function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 187.63,
          "end": 188.74,
          "en": "Let's maybe do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 188.74,
          "end": 194.68,
          "en": "Add to Cart in there, we can just call dispatch and now dispatch our own event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 194.8,
          "end": 197.57,
          "en": "Dispatch takes two important arguments here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 197.59,
          "end": 202.77,
          "en": "The first is the name of your event and that could be add to Cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 202.78,
          "end": 206.86,
          "en": "So this is the name of the event to which we can listen here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 206.86,
          "end": 211.48,
          "en": "So here I try listening to the add to cart event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 211.51,
          "end": 213.76,
          "en": "Hence we should name the event such here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 214.15,
          "end": 220.21,
          "en": "You can also optionally pass a second argument which is any event data you want to pass along.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 220.21,
          "end": 221.71,
          "en": "Something like the product ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 222.07,
          "end": 226.69,
          "en": "This can be anything can be text, it can be a number, it can be an array, it can be a JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 226.69,
          "end": 231.97,
          "en": "object, maybe something like this object with an ID of P1, whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 232,
          "end": 233.59,
          "en": "You can pass your own data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 234.1,
          "end": 240.79,
          "en": "Now we can hook up, add to cart here as a function to be executed and for delete, I'll do the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 240.79,
          "end": 241.03,
          "en": "here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 241.03,
          "end": 244.45,
          "en": "I'll just use the inline syntax to show both there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 244.45,
          "end": 246.25,
          "en": "You can also call dispatch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 246.28,
          "end": 253.64,
          "en": "I'll name the event delete because delete is also what I'm listening for here on my product component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 254.29,
          "end": 260.65,
          "en": "And again here you can also pass additional arguments like here P1, maybe just the ID as a string instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 260.65,
          "end": 262.12,
          "en": "of wrapped in an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 262.12,
          "end": 264.64,
          "en": "Again, you're free to pass any data you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 265.42,
          "end": 271.69,
          "en": "Now let me go back to App Svelte and here where I do throw this alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 272.4,
          "end": 276.27,
          "en": "Please note that we have different texts in the alerts and let's see if this now works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 276.3,
          "end": 280.74,
          "en": "If I now click Add to Cart, I see add to Cart as a text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 280.77,
          "end": 283.59000000000003,
          "en": "If I click delete I see delete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 283.74,
          "end": 290.01,
          "en": "So this is how you can emit your own custom events and this allows you to really communicate between",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 290.01,
          "end": 292.32,
          "en": "your components in a very easy way.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
